# Dial-Up

Dial-Up lets people use the internet with a phone call or SMS. A caller says a task and hangs up. An AI agent does it in a headless browser, calls back with questions if needed, then calls back with the result. Built for the c0mpiled-16 hackathon (Track 4: AI consumer products for 1 billion people; Track 2: No App). The build window is about 5.5 hours, so prefer small, working changes.

Run: `uvicorn dialup.app:app --port 8000`. Test: `python scripts/smoke_test.py`. Live view: http://localhost:8000/live.

## Architecture

```
dialup/
  app.py              create_app(): builds Services at startup, includes routers
  config.py           Settings dataclass from .env; Voice config per language (DEFAULT_VOICES)
  i18n.py             PHRASES: every caller-facing string per language; detect() for SMS
  services.py         Services container on app.state.services; services(conn) gets it
  telephony/
    routes.py         POST /voice (language menu), POST /voice/language, WS /ws, POST /sms, POST /twilio/status
    notifier.py       TwilioNotifier: ask() and send_result(), voice or SMS by task.channel
    twiml.py          relay() and sms_reply()
    security.py       twilio_form(): parses form, checks signature if VALIDATE_TWILIO
  agent/
    runner.py         Runner.start(task_id) -> background loop: Claude -> tool -> Guard
    tools.py          TOOLS schemas + Browser (Playwright page wrapper)
    guards.py         Guard: hard limits (steps, time, tokens), loop and no-effect detection
    prompts.py        system_prompt(), SUPERVISOR_WARNING, NO_TOOL_NUDGE
  tasks/
    models.py         Task, Status, Channel
    store.py          SQLite Store for tasks and events
    journal.py        Journal (log/update/status) + EventBus for the live view
    inbox.py          Inbox.ask() / deliver(): routes caller answers to the waiting task
  web/live.py         /live page, /live/stream SSE, /api/tasks
  mock_sites/bus.py   /bus demo site
scripts/smoke_test.py offline end-to-end test with ScriptedLLM and FakeCaller
```

Dependency direction: telephony and web depend on tasks and agent. agent depends on tasks. tasks depends on nothing in the app. Don't import telephony from agent; the runner reaches the caller only through the `Notifier` protocol.

## Hard rules

- Every task ends with a callback through `notifier.send_result`, for every end state: done, gave_up, stopped, failed. Never add a path that skips it.
- Record state changes through `Journal` (`log`, `update`, `status`), not by writing to `Store` directly. That keeps the live view and terminal in sync.
- Spoken or texted text: under 40 words, plain sentences, no markdown, URLs or symbols. Prices in words ("19 dollars", "19美元").
- Languages: English (`en`) and Chinese (`zh`). Never hardcode a caller-facing string in routes, runner or notifier. Add it to every language in `i18n.py` and use `phrases(task.language)`.
- Every task carries `language`. Calls to the caller pass it to `twiml.relay(settings, lang, ...)`.
- The agent never invents personal details. It uses `ask_user`.
- Agent tools stay general (goto, read_page, click, fill). Never hardcode mock-site selectors into the agent or prompts.
- Blocking SDK calls (Twilio client) go through `asyncio.to_thread`.
- Escape user text in TwiML (`quoteattr`/`escape`) and HTML (`html.escape`).
- Config comes from `Settings`. Add new settings to `config.py` and `.env.example` together. Never hardcode keys.
- Keep `scripts/smoke_test.py` passing. If you change a flow, update the test in the same change.

## ConversationRelay protocol (don't change these shapes)

Incoming: `{"type": "setup", "customParameters": {...}}`, `{"type": "prompt", "voicePrompt": "..."}`, `{"type": "error", ...}`.
Outgoing: `{"type": "text", "token": "<text>", "last": true}` to speak, `{"type": "end"}` to hang up.

Twilio does speech-to-text and text-to-speech. Don't add audio handling, Deepgram or ElevenLabs.

Call modes (customParameters.mode): `intake` (new task), `ask` (answer for task), `result` (read result, hang up). Every call also carries `lang`.

## How to add things

- New guard rule: add a check in `Guard._spinning()` (warn then stop) or `Guard.check()` (hard stop). Reasons read after "I ..." when spoken.
- New mock site: new router in `mock_sites/`, include it in `app.py`, add one line under "Sites you can use" in `prompts.py`.
- New language: a `Phrases` entry in `i18n.py`, a `Voice` entry in `DEFAULT_VOICES` in `config.py`, then add the code to `LANGUAGES` in `.env`. Add a smoke test case.
- New agent tool: schema in `TOOLS`, action in `Browser.run` (browser) or a branch in `Runner._loop` (non-browser).

## Out of scope today

Auth, multi-process scaling, Docker, a caller-facing UI, payments. Mention as future work, don't build.
